{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Step 1 (measurement): pushed as Gerrit 3455. `make verify` passed on the commit rebased onto 79f46cde8a4 (exit 0): 21483 passed / 30 skipped, integration 226 passed / 2 skipped. On macOS with `CI=1`, the spans print as expected: write_paths 2.3 s, hash_object[0..9] about 1.0-1.3 s each (even, about 57 µs per object), then unlink_paths and create_tickets. Limitation: the spans are warnings attached to the test report, so a run that times out at 600 s loses them. In that case the evidence is the crash guard's stack, which shows only the line, not the chunk index. Step 2 is planned only after a Windows sweep on main shows the spans."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795088490999579522,"uuid":"fb44465a-83b3-4ed4-ac83-5f42a46eac8f"}